# Tsakos Energy Navigation (TEN) balance sheet snapshot — METHODOLOGY §4.2, §11.6
# SHADOW DRAFT 2026-09-11 (.yaml.draft — invisible to sheet resolution; consumed
# only by scripts/shadow_regen.sh, which copies it to ten_2026-Q2.yaml inside a
# detached worktree). Record: decisions/ten_shadow_build_2026-09-11.md.
# Sources: TEN H1/Q2 2026 results release, GlobeNewswire 3359616, 2026-09-10
# ("TEN, Ltd. Reports Profits for the First Half and Second Quarter of 2026";
# rendered page saved 2026-09-11 as
# inputs/research_issuer/ten/2026-09-10_ten_h1_2026_results_pr.txt) — its
# BALANCE SHEET DATA table (In Thousands of U.S. Dollars), June 30, 2026 column —
# for every release-sourced figure; the Q1 2026 6-K ex 99.1 (EDGAR acc
# 0001193125-26-236934, filed 2026-05-22) + FY2025 20-F (acc 0001193125-26-144027,
# filed 2026-04-06) for every figure the release cannot support, KEPT at the
# 2026-Q1 sheet value and marked "UNVERIFIED (shadow)". The H1 2026 6-K was NOT
# on EDGAR at retrieval (newest TEN filing: Form 4, 2026-08-17); expected late
# Sept / early Oct 2026 (H1-2025 precedent: acc 0001193125-25-225057, filed
# 2025-09-30). Release figures are unaudited. Balance sheet date: 2026-06-30. USD.
#
# SUBSEQUENT-EVENTS AUDIT FIRST (CLAUDE.md snapshot rule; ASC/HAFN/TRMD discipline)
# — release SUBSEQUENT EVENTS / CORPORATE AFFAIRS / CORPORATE STRATEGY, 2026-09-10:
#   IN  — Ulysses (2016-built VLCC): Q1 6-K ex 99.1 SUBSEQUENT EVENTS "On May 20,
#         2026, the Company completed the sale of a 10-year-old VLCC ... about
#         $83 million in free cash after repayment of existing debt" (vessel
#         unnamed there); identity per 20-F Note 17(c) (MOA 2026-01-22, VLCC
#         Ulysses) + release CORPORATE STRATEGY "2016-built VLCC Ulysses" ->
#         "Gain on sale of vessels (37,870)" in the Q2 2026 column of STATEMENT
#         OF OPERATIONS DATA ("inclusive of $38 million capital gains"); proceeds
#         inside Cash 466,143; its held-for-sale carrying value has LEFT Other
#         assets. Gross price NOT disclosed (not promotable).
#   OUT — Anfield DP (DP2 shuttle): "on July 28, 2026, TEN took delivery of the
#         DP2 suezmax shuttle tanker Anfield DP" -> still a NEWBUILD at 6/30; its
#         instalments sit inside Advances 470,050; joins shuttle_contracted_book
#         at the Q3 refresh. Debt draw -> 6-K Note 7.
#   OUT — Alaska + Archangel (2006-built Suezmaxes): "in August 2026 TEN concluded
#         the sale of two 2006-built suezmax tankers, the Alaska and Archangel,
#         for net proceeds of $100 million" -> a sale AFTER the snapshot; owned at
#         6/30; aggregate + net, never split (do not back-solve).
#   OUT — July 2026 common dividend: "In July 2026, TEN distributed ... $1.00 per
#         share" -> post-quarter cash outflow; whether a payable sat inside Other
#         liabilities 220,881 at 6/30 is not disclosed (6-K item).
#   OUT — Series E call intent: "become redeemable at the election of the Company
#         on May 28, 2027 ... does not constitute a notice of redemption" -> E
#         still outstanding at 6/30 (13,500 H1 dividend tie, below).
#   OUT — LNG newbuild row 26 (TBN, Q1 2029) firm-up: contract undated in the
#         release (MB LNG Weekly 29, 2026-07-16 -> post-quarter if that date holds).
#   OUT — November 2026 dividend-announcement intent.
#   UNVERIFIED (shadow) — Arctic + Antarctic (2007-built Suezmaxes): repurchase
#         agreed Apr-7-2026 (Q1 6-K ex 99.1); the five-year SLB term ENDED
#         2026-06-21 (20-F leases note), BEFORE the snapshot; completion is in
#         no source on disk -> kept OUT (chartered-in, excluded) as the
#         CONSERVATIVE DEFAULT, not a prior state — see lease_liabilities. If
#         the 6-K dates completion on or before 6/30 this NAV is UNDERSTATED.
#   JUDGMENT CALL — were Alaska + Archangel HELD-FOR-SALE AT 6/30? The release has
#         no "held for sale" / MOA text and no held-for-sale line. ASSUMPTION
#         TAKEN: NOT held-for-sale at 6/30 -> on-curve in the manifest draft,
#         inside "Vessels, net", NOT inside the WC composite. This is the
#         NON-CONSERVATIVE side (verifier 2026-09-11): if the pair was HFS at
#         6/30 its carrying value already sits inside Other assets 286,240 (the
#         Ulysses precedent) and the on-curve marks double-count it. Why taken:
#         (i) no MOA date exists for this pair in any source on disk — the 9/01
#         PR (GlobeNewswire 3354219, inputs/earnings_calendar.yaml TEN basis;
#         text not on disk, ten_log entry owed; WebFetch 2026-09-11 reads only
#         "TEN announced today the sale of two 2006-built Suezmax tankers. This
#         transaction will release in excess of $100 million to the company's
#         cash reserves" — no agreement date, neither "agreed" nor "concluded")
#         and the 9/10 release (SUBSEQUENT EVENTS: "in August 2026 TEN
#         concluded the sale") both post-date the quarter; under ASC
#         360-10-45-9 a signed MOA normally
#         meets the held-for-sale criteria, but TEN discloses no classification
#         policy (20-F Note 17(c) says only that an MOA was signed for Ulysses;
#         the Ulysses HFS-at-Mar-31 treatment was the Q1 prereg's inference from
#         the Other-assets swing, not a disclosed policy); (ii) the release's
#         Vessels, net bridge (3,145,164 -> 3,155,282, +10,118, net of 46,295
#         D&A and no NB delivery) is NON-DISCRIMINATING: a 6/30 HFS reclass of
#         two 20-year-old hulls would move only their (undisclosed, small)
#         carrying value — not the $100M net proceeds — and the unidentified Q2
#         additions of roughly $52-56M have a named candidate (the Apr-7
#         Arctic/Antarctic repurchase, itself UNVERIFIED); (iii) the default for
#         a row the sources do not move is its prior state (owned, on-curve).
#         The call rests on (i) and (iii). EXPOSURE if wrong, bounded: the
#         pair's on-curve marks at 20.35/20.45y on the txn-anchored Suezmax
#         curve are about $61M = about $2.0/sh (base curve about $67M); the
#         20-F carrying basis is smaller still (repurchased Jul-19/Aug-22-2024
#         at $21,000K each net of the $5,900K seller's credit; finance-lease
#         liability remeasured $43,316K incl. the $11,800K credit — 20-F leases
#         note). FLIPS on a 6-K vessels-held-for-sale note dating an MOA on or
#         before 2026-06-30: rows out of the manifest, carrying value inside
#         Other assets (Ulysses precedent), held_for_sale stays 0 — this
#         composite would NOT change, only the manifest would.
#
# TEN is the first **3-sleeve hybrid** + first name with `shuttle_contracted_book`
# populated (METHODOLOGY §11.6 off-curve-at-contracted-book convention).

ticker: TEN
quarter: 2026-Q2
