# Preferred equity + NCI (METHODOLOGY §4.2; NCI via preferred_equity since the
# 2026-07-15 reconciliation — the BWLP convention):
#   - Series E: 4,745,947 shares × $25.00 redemption value = $118,649K (20-F)
#                9.25% coupon, dividends 28-Feb/May/Aug/Nov
#   - Series F: 6,747,147 shares × $25.00 redemption value = $168,679K (20-F)
#                9.50% coupon, dividends 30-Jan/Apr/Jul/Oct
#   Total liquidation preference: $287,328K — RE-TIED by the release (2026-09-10):
#   "Effect of preferred dividends (6,750)" per quarter / "(13,500)" H1 2026 =
#   118,649 × 9.25%/2 + 168,679 × 9.50%/2 = 13,500, both series outstanding at
#   6/30. Series E call intent (CORPORATE AFFAIRS): "become redeemable at the
#   election of the Company on May 28, 2027 ... may elect to redeem, all or a
#   portion ... does not constitute a notice of redemption" -> no change at 6/30.
# (Tsakos-affiliated entities hold 45,000 Series E + 100,000 Series F per 20-F.)
# PLUS non-controlling interest — the BWLP NCI-via-preferred_equity convention:
#   49% of Mare Success S.A. (owns Selini, Salamina, Byzantion, Bosporos — all
#   four consolidated at 100% in the fleet manifest) is held by Polaris Oil
#   Shipping (Flopec affiliate), 20-F Note 11. Book basis ROLLED on the 2026-Q1
#   construction (audited + attributable income; FY2025 zero distributions per
#   the 20-F): Dec-31-2025 audited $43,529K + Q1-2026 attributable $2,425K (Q1
#   6-K) + Q2-2026 attributable $4,176K (release 2026-09-10 STATEMENT OF
#   OPERATIONS: "Less: Net income attributable to the noncontrolling interest
#   (4,176)" Q2; "(6,601)" H1 = 2,425 + 4,176, ties) = $50,130K.
#   UNVERIFIED (shadow) on the distribution leg: the roll treats Q2
#   distributions to Polaris as zero (the same basis the Q1 sheet used); awaits
#   the 6-K noncontrolling-interest note / Mare Success distributions.
#   JUDGMENT CALL 2026-09-11 (verifier, snapshot lens): rolling is the
#   CONSERVATIVE side (more NCI subtracted; holding 45,954 would be +4,176
#   non-conservative, about +$0.14/sh) and keeps the Q1 construction.
#   NAV-basis derivation still not disclosed-derivable (sub-level debt/cash
#   unknown) — owner fork decisions/ten_reconciliation_prereg_2026-07-15.md §6.1.
#   287,328 + 50,130 = 337,458 (2026-Q1 sheet: 287,328 + 45,954 = 333,282)
preferred_equity: 337458000

# Governance / structural-NAV-trap discount (METHODOLOGY §15, NEW 2026-06-06):
# TEN is the framework's first §15 case — a controlled FPI structure where
# the market consistently applies a 50-60% P/NAV discount. Drivers per
# external read + user analysis:
#   - Controlled-shareholder structure (Tsakos family); related-party
#     transactions including management fees to Tsakos Columbia Shipmanagement
#   - Low common payout: $1.50/share against ~$8 EPS in 2026 (~19% payout
#     ratio); 36% YoY increase is "highest dividend in 10 years" but still
#     well below mainstream tanker-cycle peers (DHT/NAT 100%, FRO 80%)
#   - No buyback program; retained capital deployed into a $2.4B NB orderbook
#     whose returns to common are uncertain
#   - Preferred E+F structure ($287M aggregate) with Tsakos-affiliated owners
#     holding meaningful slugs (0.95% E + 1.5% F per 20-F)
#
# 30% NAV haircut chosen to bring tool PW FV into the neighborhood of VIE
# Bullish $51.50 — i.e., interpret VIE's already-discounted target as the
# anchor for what the market will pay rather than what the assets are worth.
# Conservative read: even VIE Bullish applies ~47% discount vs unconstrained
# NAV; our 30% sits in between full-realisation (0%) and VIE Bullish (47%),
# allowing room for partial governance improvement vs full continuation of
# the historical discount. Judgmental; revisit when governance signals shift
# (e.g., capital-return policy change, management transition, M&A).
#
# Applied at the BLEND layer (NAV term) and on the strip's TERMINAL value —
# both are NAV-realisation computations. Interim DPS are NOT haircut (already-
# realised cash to common). Broker-NAV sweep operates on undiscounted NAV
# (the question "what are the assets worth" is independent of "what will
# common shareholders capture").
#
# SHADOW 2026-09-11 — HOLD 0.30 per decisions/ten_h1_release_check_2026-09-10.md
# §6 (§15.7 working band 30-36%): the release carries no related-party fee
# figure (only the footnote that overhead "include[s] Management fees"), no
# buyback, unquantified NB commitments; payout $1.50 on H1-2026-annualised EPS
# 14.24 = 10.5% (worse than the 19% in the rationale above), against the new
# Series E call intent (May 28, 2027, mildly positive for common). Nothing
# moves the haircut out of band; revisit at the 6-K related-party note / the
# November 2026 dividend announcement. Judgmental HOLD, not a sourced figure.
governance_discount_pct: 0.30

# Shuttle contracted-book (METHODOLOGY §11.6, NEW 2026-06-05 PM): NPV of the 4
# in-water DP2 shuttle tankers at contracted day rates + Suezmax-curve residual
# at TC expiry, discounted at WACC 11%, utilization 98.3%, offhire 1%, daily opex
# $11,000/day (~10% premium over conventional Suezmax) — carried UNCHANGED from
# the 2026-Q1 sheet. Anfield DP (delivered July 28, 2026 per the release
# SUBSEQUENT EVENTS; "10-year employment to a US oil major, with charter options
# to extend the charter until the vessel's 20th year anniversary"; "the expected
# gross revenues should approach $500 million" at maximum duration — an
# envelope, NOT a day rate) is OUT of the 6/30 snapshot and joins this book at
# the Q3 refresh.
#
# Per-vessel breakdown (npv = revenue NPV − opex NPV + residual NPV @ TC expiry):
#   Brasil 2014   $104.8M  ($58,908/d → $60k extension; ext to 2033-11; age 20.5; residual $14.7M NPV)
#   Rio 2016      $104.2M  ($58,403/d → $60k extension; ext to 2033-10; age 20.6; residual $14.6M NPV)
#   Athens 04     $121.5M  ($58,569/d through 2032-05; age 7.0; residual $45.4M NPV; high residual)
#   Paris 24      $122.6M  ($58,569/d through 2032-08; age 6.9; residual $44.4M NPV; high residual)
#   --
#   TOTAL         $453.1M
#
# Extension rates ($60k/day for Brasil/Rio) are an APPROX of "increased rate"
# disclosed in the Q1 6-K subsequent events (April 23, 2026). Material if the
# actual rate is materially higher; the methodology underweights the extension
# value, leaving upside if the disclosure resolves favorably.
# UNVERIFIED (shadow): awaits an extension-rate disclosure (6-K / data kit) —
# the release carries no Brasil/Rio rate. NPV struck at the Q1 build (as-of
# 2026-03-31) and NOT re-struck at 6/30: the ages inside the breakdown are the
# Q1 build's, and one quarter of contracted margin (4 hulls x 91 days x ($58.5k
# rate less $11k opex) x 0.983 utilisation, about $17M) has been collected
# into Cash 466,143 while still counted inside this NPV; net of the 11% unwind
# (about $12M) the overlap is about $5M (about $0.15/sh), NON-CONSERVATIVE.
# Re-strike the book at the live land (the Q3 refresh also adds Anfield DP).
shuttle_contracted_book: 453100000

# held_for_sale: key deliberately ABSENT (loader default 0), as in the 2026-Q1
# sheet (decisions/ten_reconciliation_prereg_2026-07-15.md §2 ruled "0
# (deliberate)"): Ulysses is sold; Alaska + Archangel are carried as owned and
# operating at 6/30 (header judgment call — their HFS status at 6/30 is
# UNVERIFIED (shadow), awaits the 6-K vessels-held-for-sale / subsequent-events
# note), and even under the flip case their carrying value sits inside the WC
# composite (Ulysses precedent), not here.
